From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: krane <chris@krane.dev>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 16:01:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(thumbnails): hash wallpaper paths without resolving
 symlinks

Local fix (not a pctrade/end4-pC backport)
Problem: generate-thumbnails-magick.sh named thumbnails after the symlink target, while the wallpaper selector looks them up by the listed path, so symlinked wallpapers (home-manager puts them in /nix/store) never showed a thumbnail.
Port: local
Drop when: the pinned thumbnail scripts hash the listed path, not its realpath.
---
 .../ii/scripts/thumbnails/generate-thumbnails-magick.sh        | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/scripts/thumbnails/generate-thumbnails-magick.sh b/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/scripts/thumbnails/generate-thumbnails-magick.sh
index 3c464601..8571c24d 100755
--- a/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/scripts/thumbnails/generate-thumbnails-magick.sh
+++ b/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/scripts/thumbnails/generate-thumbnails-magick.sh
@@ -46,7 +46,8 @@ urlencode() {
 generate_thumbnail() {
     local src="$1"
     local abs_path
-    abs_path="$(realpath "$src")"
+    # -s/--no-symlinks: the selector's ThumbnailImage hashes the path as listed, not its symlink target
+    abs_path="$(realpath -s "$src")"
     # Skip files with multiple frames (GIFs, videos, etc.)
     case "${abs_path,,}" in
         *.gif|*.mp4|*.webm|*.mkv|*.avi|*.mov)
